  "body": "Consider a page hosted on `https://www.gourmet.com.s3-website-us-east-1.amazonaws.com` that does `document.domain = \"amazonaws.com\"`.\r\n\r\n`amazonaws.com` itself is not in the PSL. `s3-website-us-east-1.amazonaws.com` is.\r\n\r\nLet's walk through the algorithms:\r\n\r\n- [`document.domain` setter](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/origin.html#dom-document-domain) with `\"amazonaws.com\"` calls\r\n- [is a registrable domain suffix of or is equal to](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/origin.html#is-a-registrable-domain-suffix-of-or-is-equal-to) with _hostSuffixString_ = `\"amazonaws.com\"`, _originalHost_ = `www.gourmet.com.s3-website-us-east-1.amazonaws.com`, which calls\r\n- [public suffix](https://url.spec.whatwg.org/#host-public-suffix) with `amazonaws.com`, which calls\r\n- [PSL algorithm](https://publicsuffix.org/list/) with `amazonaws.com`, which returns `com`\r\n\r\nSince `com` is not equal to `amazonaws.com`, all the checks succeed, and `document.domain` setting works. This is not as intended!\r\n\r\n@sleevi suggests that the correct algorithm is instead something like this:\r\n\r\n* Let _originalSuffix_ equal _originalHost_'s public suffix.\r\n* If _host_ is equals _originalSuffix_, then return false.\r\n* If _host_ is shorter than _originalSuffix_, then return false. (this step would catch the above)\r\n* If _host_ equals _host_'s public suffix, then return false.\r\n* If _originalSuffix_, prefixed by a U+002E FULL STOP, exactly matches the end of _host_, then return true.",
